  "lineage": "Six-maqam classical suite cycle of Bukhara and Samarkand, formalized at the Bukharan emir's court in the 18th-19th centuries and notated in the 1920s-50s by Viktor Uspensky and Yunus Rajabiy — each maqam opening with an instrumental mushkilot section on tanbur and dutar in fixed doira usul cycles, then a vocal nasr section whose successive shu'ba climb stepwise to the awj apex on Persian and Hebrew-inflected Chagatai poetry before the descent (furovard).",
